(Remote work) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Employees may work from home up to three days per week after completing their probation period.) Tj T*
(During probation, new employees work from the office every day so they can learn from their) Tj T*
(team.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Remote workers must be available on the company chat during core hours and must join video) Tj T*
(meetings with their camera on when presenting. The company provides a laptop and a monthly) Tj T*
(internet allowance of 1,500 rupees for remote work.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Working from another country requires written approval from HR at least 30 days before travel,) Tj T*
(because of tax and data protection rules.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
( Probation) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Every new employee has a probation period of six months. Halfway through, your manager holds a) Tj T*
(review meeting to discuss your progress. At the end of probation, you receive a written) Tj T*
(confirmation of your permanent position or, in rare cases, an extension of up to three months.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
