(Leave) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(New employees receive 15 days of paid annual leave in their first year. From the second year,) Tj T*
(annual leave increases to 20 days. Up to 5 unused days can be carried over to the next year;) Tj T*
(any remaining days expire on 31 March.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Leave requests must be submitted in the HR portal at least two weeks in advance for absences) Tj T*
(longer than three days. Your manager approves or rejects the request within five working days.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Sick leave is paid in full for up to 12 days per year. If you are sick for more than two) Tj T*
(consecutive days, you must upload a doctor's note to the HR portal.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Parents receive 26 weeks of paid maternity leave or 4 weeks of paid paternity leave. Adoption) Tj T*
(leave follows the same rules as maternity and paternity leave.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
( Expenses and travel) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Business travel must be booked through the company travel portal. Economy class is used for) Tj T*
(flights shorter than six hours; business class may be approved by a director for longer) Tj T*
(flights.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Meal expenses during business travel are reimbursed up to 2,000 rupees per day. Keep all) Tj T*
(receipts and submit your expense report within 30 days of returning. Reports submitted later) Tj T*
(than 60 days are not reimbursed.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
